-- title:
--   Full Slice ABAB Scalar To BABAtensor
-- statement:
--   **The full-slice scalar quartic is close to the $BAB\otimes A$ tensor form.**
--
--   Let $(q,m,d)$ have a field model, let $S$ be a symmetric strategy on the successor space, and let `family` be a slice-indexed polynomial submeasurement family. Assume that the state is normalized and that `family` is strongly self-consistent in $S$ with error $\zeta$. The full-slice scalar $\mathrm{ABAB}$ average and the corresponding full-slice $BAB\otimes A$ tensor average obey
--
--   $$
--   \left|
--   \mathrm{fullSliceABABAvg}(S,\mathrm{family})
--   -\mathrm{fullSliceBABAtensorAvg}(S,\mathrm{family})
--   \right|
--   \le \sqrt{\zeta}.
--   $$
--
--   This is the scalar-to-tensor comparison for the paper's commutativity estimate at `eq:gcom4`. It is used in the subsequent bridge from the full-slice quartic to the x-evaluated tensor endpoint.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.Commutativity.fullSliceABAB_scalar_to_BABAtensor`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
